{"_meta":{"source":"Yahoo Finance via yfinance (profile, statements, analyst estimates)","fetched_at":"2026-10-29T07:37:47+00:00","status":"ok","error":null,"last_success":"2026-10-29T07:37:47+00:00"},"data":{"profile":{"name":"Meta Platforms, Inc.","sector":"Communication Services","industry":"Internet Content & Information","country":"United States","city":"Menlo Park","website":"https://www.meta.com","employees":66775,"summary":"Meta Platforms, Inc. engages in the development of products that enable people to connect and share with friends and family through mobile devices, personal computers, virtual reality (VR) headsets, and AI glasses in the United States, Canada, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and internationally. It operates through two segments, Family of Apps (FoA) and Reality Labs (RL). The FoA segment offers Facebook, which enables people to build community through feed, reels, stories, groups, marketplace, and other; Instagram that brings people closer through Instagram feed, stories, reels, live, and messaging; Messenger, a messaging application for people to connect with friends, family, communities, and businesses across platforms and devices through text, audio, and video calls; Meta AI, an assistant that's available across apps, as a stand-alone app, on AI glasses, and on the web; Threads, an application for text-based updates and public conversations; and WhatsApp, a messaging application that is used by people and businesses to communicate and transact. The RL segment provides virtual and augmented reality products, including consumer hardware, software, and content that help people feel connected, as well as Meta Quest devices that enable social experiences across gaming, fitness, entertainment, and more. The segment also includes wearables such as AI glasses like Ray Ban Meta and Oakley Meta glasses; and the Meta Ray Ban Display, which combines AI glasses with an integrated lens display and the Meta Neural Band, a wrist worn device using electromyography that lets people control their AI glasses through neuromuscular signals. Meta Platforms, Inc. has a collaboration with Microsoft Corporation, NVIDIA Corporation, Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Broadcom Inc., and OpenAI, L.L.C. The company was formerly known as Facebook, Inc. and changed its name to Meta Platforms, Inc. in October 2021. The company was incorporated in 2004 and is headquartered in Menlo Park, California.","exchange":"NasdaqGS","currency":"USD","financial_currency":"USD","summary_fr":"Meta Platforms, Inc. s'engage dans le développement de produits qui permettent aux gens de se connecter et de partager avec leurs amis et leur famille via des appareils mobiles, des ordinateurs personnels, des casques de réalité virtuelle (VR) et des lunettes d'IA aux États-Unis, au Canada, en Europe, en Asie-Pacifique et à l'international. Il opère à travers deux segments, Family of Apps (FoA) et Reality Labs (RL). Le segment FoA propose Facebook, qui permet aux gens de créer une communauté via des flux, des rouleaux, des histoires, des groupes, des marchés et autres; Instagram qui rapproche les gens via des flux, des histoires, des rouleaux, des live et des messages; Messenger, une application de messagerie permettant aux gens de se connecter avec leurs amis, leur famille, leurs communautés et leurs entreprises à travers des plateformes et des appareils via des appels texte, audio et vidéo; Le segment RL fournit des produits de réalité virtuelle et augmentée, y compris du matériel, des logiciels et du contenu grand public qui aident les gens à se sentir connectés, ainsi que des appareils Meta Quest qui permettent des expériences sociales dans les domaines du jeu, du fitness, du divertissement et plus encore. Le segment comprend également des dispositifs portables tels que des lunettes AI comme les lunettes Ray Ban Meta et Oakley Meta; et le Meta Ray Ban Display, qui combine des lunettes AI avec un écran de lentille intégré et le Meta Neural Band, un appareil porté au poignet utilisant l'électromyographie qui permet aux gens de contrôler leurs lunettes AI par des signaux neuromusculaires. Meta Platforms, Inc. collabore avec Microsoft Corporation, NVIDIA Corporation, Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Broadcom Inc. et OpenAI, L.L.C. La société était auparavant connue sous le nom de Facebook, Inc. et a changé son nom pour Meta Platforms, Inc. en octobre 2021. La société a été constituée en 2004 et a son siège social à Menlo Park, en Californie."},"valuation":{"market_cap_yahoo":1594209206272,"shares_outstanding":2260455318,"trailing_pe":20.896963,"forward_pe":17.425035,"price_to_book":5.7474637,"ev_to_ebitda":13.754,"ev_to_revenue":6.614,"dividend_yield":0.0033000002,"payout_ratio":0.0716,"beta_yahoo":1.185},"targets":{"current_price":612.49,"mean":848.3765,"median":850.0,"high":1050.0,"low":629.06,"n_analysts":58,"reco_mean":1.40323,"reco_key":"strong_buy"},"calendar":{"earnings_dates":["2026-10-21"],"eps_avg":8.554,"eps_low":7.64,"eps_high":9.65,"revenue_avg":75120697740,"ex_dividend":"2026-09-21","dividend_date":"2026-09-28"},"holders":{"insiders_pct":0.00147,"institutions_pct":0.78861,"institutions_float_pct":0.78976995,"institutions_n":6628,"institutions":[{"name":"Blackrock Inc.","pct":0.0783,"shares":173396976,"value":106203912136,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.027},{"name":"Vanguard Capital Management LLC","pct":0.0648,"shares":143440997,"value":87856174851,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0092},{"name":"FMR, LLC","pct":0.0433,"shares":95895744,"value":58735183306,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":-0.1777},{"name":"State Street Corporation","pct":0.0416,"shares":92033963,"value":56369881099,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0397},{"name":"Geode Capital Management, LLC","pct":0.0248,"shares":54949893,"value":33656259426,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":0.0145000005},{"name":"JPMORGAN CHASE & CO","pct":0.0207,"shares":45944387,"value":28140477144,"date":"2026-06-30","chg":-0.0844},{"name":"Capital World Investors","pct":0.0185,"shares":40876883,"value":250366